    "exit_rule": "Every deployable in FD-001 must have reproducible cloud-native Kubernetes deployment evidence across Talos, Ubuntu LTS, Debian, Fedora Server, Oracle Linux, RHEL-compatible, CentOS Stream, Rocky Linux, AlmaLinux, SUSE Linux Enterprise, and macOS Apple Silicon targets. Product code cannot depend on a host distribution or desktop OS; OS-specific bootstrap belongs in adapter packs. Talos-class nodes must support remote setup by pointing at a signed, policy-validated configuration artifact that lets them securely join the cluster with identity, mTLS or equivalent trust, and auditable join evidence; secret material must be externalized from the repo and delivered through approved secret stores or sealed bootstrap channels. For any supported target machine that satisfies declared hardware, network, identity, and trust prerequisites, a one-time script launch or one-click setup must converge the machine into a secured, hardened cluster member with production hardening baselines, cluster membership, policy compliance, observability enrollment, audit enrollment, and generated evidence. If prerequisites are not met, the setup must fail closed without partial production enrollment and emit an actionable evidence report. macOS Apple Silicon support is proven through arm64 OCI images and local Kubernetes/OCI parity evidence, not host-specific product code. Production images default to distroless or scratch where technically viable, with full-base-image exceptions allowed only through evidence of runtime necessity, explicit owner approval, SBOM, image-size and vulnerability budgets, and a removal/optimization follow-up. Accepted deployment evidence requires declarative OpenTofu/IaC, GitOps manifests, portable Kubernetes manifests or Helm/Kustomize overlays, OCI images, SBOM/provenance attestations, cluster conformance results, one-command or one-click setup entrypoints, generated bootstrap evidence, secure cluster-join evidence, and restore evidence. Manual SSH snowflakes or unrecorded mutable hosts block planning closure."
